        <span class="eyebrow">Why this book</span>
        <h2 id="shift-title" class="h2">The ground is <em>shifting.</em></h2>
        <p class="lede">
          It started with porting the Claude Agent SDK from Python to Go — using Claude Code itself.
          Over a hundred prompts, and one realisation: most of them were wasted, because I didn't yet know how to
          <em>direct</em> the work. Not because the model wasn't smart enough. Because I wasn't.
        </p>
        <ul class="shift__points">
          <li><span>i</span><div><h3>The craft is molting, not dying</h3><p>The keystrokes and boilerplate fall away. Systems thinking, taste, and judgement become the whole game.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>ii</span><div><h3>Nobody handed us a playbook</h3><p>The tools arrived faster than the practices. This is the honest engineering guide — no hype, no doom, real scar tissue.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>iii</span><div><h3>The boring things win</h3><p>Context, guardrails, tests, conventions. Tools change every quarter. Those compound over a career.</p></div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
